        "title": "Natural Fibers - Plant (Cellulosic)",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nALL PLANT FIBERS = CELLULOSE POLYMER\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                                                                  |\n|   β-D-glucose monomer    (C₆H₁₀O₅)                               |\n|        ↓                                                         |\n|   β-1,4-glycosidic linkage (not α-1,4 like starch)               |\n|        ↓                                                         |\n|   Linear cellulose chains (degree of polymerization 1,000–15,000)|\n|        ↓                                                         |\n|   Hydrogen bonding between chains                                |\n|        ↓ ↓                                                       |\n|  Crystalline regions     Amorphous regions                       |\n|  (strong, rigid,         (flexible, accessible                   |\n|   hydrophobic)            to water, dyeable)                     |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------+"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-NATURAL-FIBERS-PLANT.md#003",
      "path": [
        "01-NATURAL-FIBERS-PLANT.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
