        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Why cellulose feels good against skin: the hydroxyl (-OH) groups make it hydrophilic — it absorbs moisture from sweat, then releases it to air. Cotton at 7% moisture regain; linen at ~12%. This is why linen is cooler-feeling than cotton — better thermal conductivity when moist."
    },
