        "title": "Natural Fibers - Plant (Cellulosic)",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "GINNING (separating fiber from seed)\n  Saw gin (post-Whitney, dominant): rotating saw teeth pull fiber\n  through slots too narrow for seed; ~200 bales/day machine\n  Roller gin (older, for long-staple): gentler, avoids fiber nep"
    },
    {
