        "section": "textiles",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Natural Fibers - Plant (Cellulosic)",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "MECHANISM:\n  1. Gin makes short-staple cotton profitable → expand cotton cultivation\n  2. Cotton cultivation required intensive hand labor for weeding, thinning,\n     picking (gin solved ginning, not growing/picking)\n  3. Slavery was the labor source → slavery expansion, not contraction,\n     was the economic logic after the gin"
    }
